  "title": "Thermal Loom",
  "rules": [
    "Four pieces pass through press, furnace and quench to shipping. Three shipments complete the task.",
    "Only the corresponding specialist loads each machine; everyone can carry, drop, hand off, ship and crank.",
    "Processing needs three, four and two powered ticks. Outputs must be removed before a machine reloads.",
    "At most two machines receive power each tick using rotating priority, spending one common charge per powered machine.",
    "Generator cranking adds four charge, capped at twenty-four; recycling scrap adds three.",
    "Hot furnace output has eighteen ticks to finish quenching. Stored, carried and processing hot items all face expiry.",
    "Two narrow crossings and exclusive worker cells create congestion; following into a just-vacated cell fails.",
    "Three shipments or insufficient remaining viable material ends naturally; otherwise step 128 truncates."
  ],
